{
    "background_story": "Alejandra was a free-spirited artist, known for her breathtakingly beautiful installations that seemed to capture the essence of the ephemeral nature of life. Her art was a reflection of her own transitory existence, as she traveled from place to place, never staying in one spot for too long. With each new location, she would create a new piece, using materials that were readily available and often impermanent. Her art was a whispered promise, a fleeting glimpse into the beauty of the present moment. As quickly as her installations appeared, they would vanish, leaving behind only memories and the faint scent of their existence. Alejandra's art was a reminder to cherish the ephemeral nature of life, to appreciate the beauty that surrounds us, and to never take anything for granted.",
